# The stem's files this node carries MODIFIED, each with the reason it differs.
#
# WHAT THIS IS FOR. `.offshoot-omissions` lists what this repo does not carry
# from its stem (jolly-roger `integration`); this lists what it carries and
# changes. Everything else is the stem's byte for byte or this repo's own, so a
# diff against the stem reads as: the additions, the omissions (listed there)
# and these. A modified file is a conflict on every cascade that touches it, so
# each one here is a cost paid on purpose, and the reason says what it buys. A
# cascade reviewer meeting one of these files knows the node's side is a
# decision; meeting any other modified file, it is drift.
#
# AND IT IS CHECKED, by `scripts/check-divergences.mjs` (the tree's one copy,
# from template-svelte), run by `web/test/offshoot-divergences.test.ts` and by
# `scripts/apply-omissions.sh` during a merge: it fails on a modified file with
# no entry, on an entry whose file no longer differs, and on an entry with no
# reason. A file at the stem's OLD version is drift, not a divergence:
# `scripts/check-stem-drift.mjs` catches that.
#
# FORMAT. One file per line: its path, then its reason. `#` starts a comment.
# A line `[<branch>]` starts a section.
#
# THIS REPO'S LIST IS ITS OWN. Its stem repo keeps a list too, and a cascade
# that changes it conflicts here: keep this side, always (the stem's entries
# describe the stem, not this repo), as `.offshoot-omissions` says of omissions.
#
# ONE SECTION, with no marker: this repo has one branch, `main`, fed from
# jolly-roger `integration`. duel-in-the-dark, its child repo, keeps a list of
# its own.

